# SaaS Factory

You are operating inside a SaaS Factory system.

## Rules

- Follow agent role definitions under **`factory/02_workforce/02_00_agents/agent_definitions/`** when the user invokes a role: pm, builder, dev, quality, fix, git, spec-generator, architect, security, devops, docs, support, tooling, finops, spike, broadcasting (see `organizational_memory/AGENTS.md` for when to use each). **Shorthand:** `.cursor/commands/agent-*.md` / `@factory/02_workforce/02_00_agents/agent_definitions/<role>-agent.md`. Capabilities + routing: **`factory/02_workforce/02_00_agents/agent-registry.json`**; structured outputs: `factory/factory_schemas/`; validate JSON: `npm run mfg -- validate agent-output`. For flow, WIP, and waste reduction, align with `organizational_memory/LEAN-MANUFACTURING.md` when the user asks for lean / process improvements.
- **Resources manifest (every agent turn):** When the user invokes an agent role (`@…/agent_definitions/…`), **begin the response** with the **Resources & dependencies** block defined in `organizational_memory/AGENTS.md` (materials, permits, gates — inputs, tools, access, other agents, blockers). Then proceed with role work. Skip only if the user explicitly waives it for that message.
- **Verticals** ship as **`apps/<vertical>-instance/`** with optional shared **`packages/*`** per `organizational_memory/ARCHITECTURE.md` — respect **integration mode** there (**monorepo-integrated** vs **HTTP-integrated** vs **standalone**) when adding frontend/backend code or cross-app calls. Do not collapse into a single config-only runtime unless the user explicitly asks to change that decision.
- Do not mix responsibilities between agents; stay in the role the user invoked.
- All work must be traceable to a task `id` from `factory/03_assembly_lines/03-registry/registry/task-queue.json` or PM output when the user provides one.
- Prefer creating or updating files with minimal, targeted edits; do not rewrite large files blindly.
- **Bulk repo search for shell pipelines** (`sed`/`perl`/renames): use **`grep -rl`** (POSIX); do **not** assume **`rg`** is installed. See **`factory/README.md`** → *Bulk search / replace*.
- **Harness and verification** (local/CI fixtures, mocks, seeds, build/tests, acceptance) are owned by **`factory/02_workforce/02_00_agents/agent_definitions/quality-agent.md`** (partner to Dev); treat features as incomplete until Quality criteria there are satisfied (or explicitly waived by the user).
- If requirements are unclear, stop and ask for clarification before large changes.
- When an agent role **performed substantive repo work**, it should leave a structured **QMS inbox record** per **`factory/02_workforce/02_00_agents/agent_definitions/agent-record-for-qms.md`** under `organizational_memory/QMS/inbox/`. **Docs Agent** consolidates selected records into ISO-style **controlled documents** under `organizational_memory/QMS/published/` and updates `organizational_memory/QMS/LESSONS-LEARNED.md` (see **`factory/02_workforce/02_00_agents/agent_definitions/docs-agent.md`**).
- **IV&V-style controlled procedures** (SE V-model parity, informative): `organizational_memory/QMS/published/QMS-PUB-001-system-validation-strategy.md` (validation), `QMS-PUB-002-system-verification-plan.md` (system verification / acceptance), `QMS-PUB-003-subsystem-verification-plan.md` (subsystem acceptance), `QMS-PUB-004-unit-device-test-plan.md` (unit / device tests). Index: `organizational_memory/QMS/README.md`; registry: `organizational_memory/QMS/DOCUMENT-CONTROL.md`; machine pointer: **`factory/02_workforce/02_00_agents/agent-registry.json`** → `references.qms_ivv_procedures`.
